  urldate = {2025-07-18},
  abstract = {The present study estimates methane (CH4) emissions from rice cultivation in the Vietnamese Mekong Delta (VMD) using Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-5P satellite datasets in Google Earth Engine platform. A rule-based classifier was employed to identify seasonal rice-cultivated areas for generating seasonal CH4 emission maps. The initial findings reveal that the upper region of the delta, characterized by deep flooding, is a primary rice-producing area, with the majority of cultivation occurring during the winter-spring season. While CH4 emissions did not exhibit substantial seasonal variations, higher emissions are observed in the deep-flooded zones. This research provides valuable insights into the spatiotemporal dynamics of CH4 emissions (2021-2022) from rice cultivation in the VMD, aiding in developing targeted mitigation strategies to address climate change.},
