  urldate = {2025-09-04},
  abstract = {The Mekong River Delta in Vietnam (VMD) is the largest agricultural and aqua-cultural production region in Vietnam. However, the delta is experiencing several environmental issues comprising polluted surface waters, loss of biodiversity, and degraded ecosystem functions and then poses a risk to the livelihood of local people who depend mainly on the services provided by the Mekong River and its tributaries. This chapter reviews the major stressors evolving from natural and anthropogenic sources driving the damages on surface water in VMD over the two last decades. Besides, the impacts of pollutants on ecosystems, livelihoods, and human health were also mentioned. Finally, possible measures could be implemented by the sectors in order to enhance the sustainability of the water in the Mekong River Delta.},
