  abstract = {The paper aims to present the water quality status in Vam Co Dong river, the section flowing in Tay Ninh province. The results show that the water quality in the area has polluting substances concentration such as Fe, nutrient (NH4+, PO4 3-), organic matter (COD, BOD ), coliform bacteria exceeding QCVN 08-MT: 2015/BTNMT, column A2, particually in the rainy season. The research also calculates WQI in the area, showing that river can be a source of water for domestic purposes with appropriate handling measures and the rivers water receiving capacity according to the guidance of Circular No.76/2017/TT-BTNMT, with the loads of COD, TSS, Ammonium and total P at -44,001.7 kg/day, -147,370.85 kg/day, -2,131.3 kg/day and -185,955 kg/day respectively, so Vam Co Dong is only capable of receiving BOD5 parameter. In order to protect the water quality, there is a need to increasingly monitor waste sources to Vam Co Dong river.},
